window.PH_INDEX = [{"t":"Store packs","u":"admin/c_store_packs.html","d":"A store pack puts one store's own produce codes into its cashiers' copies of PLUed. You build it in the Store Pack Builder, a free page that runs in a web browser.","b":"store packs a store pack puts one store's own produce codes into its cashiers' copies of plued . you build it in the store pack builder , a free page that runs in a web browser. a pack is optional. plued teaches the standard produce codes with no pack at all. a pack adds the local layer: the sizes your store stocks, the codes only your register uses, and the drills you want new hires to start with. what a pack carries store name the name cashiers see on the store's card in the app. codes each code with its item name, its category (fruit, vegetable or other) and, when it matters, its size. a code can be a standard plu or one of the store's own codes of 3 to 5 digits. sections the aisle each code belongs to, such as citrus or a section you name yourself. practice lists optional groups of items to drill together, such as a front table or a new hire's first week. pictures one picture from the plued catalog for each code. you never upload a picture. for an item the catalog does not show, you pick the closest picture and can request a new one. a pack can also carry a second name for the store, each code, each section and each practice list, so that a cashier whose phone is set to that language sees those names. the builder the store pack builder opens at plued.app /pack . it is free and needs no account. it keeps your draft in the browser you work in, so the pack is still there when you come back on the same computer. the builder walks you through four steps: name your store , add your codes , practice lists and share with your team . how cashiers receive a pack when you share a pack, the builder gives you a link and a qr code. a cashier scans the qr code with the phone's camera or taps the link, and the app imports the pack. a cashier who is already in the app can open library > import pack and scan the qr code, paste the link, or open a .plupack file. the phone needs a connection the first time. after the import, the cashier has a card on home titled with your store's name, your items in the library under my store , and your practice lists as named collections under your store's name. the standard codes stay in the app beside yours. any cashier can import a pack and look through it for free. practicing it needs the cashier's one-time unlock or your store's code from a store plan. note: level 1, pluzzle , the density score and the nutrition tools are free. other study needs the one-time unlock or a store code."},{"t":"Store Plans and store codes","u":"admin/c_store_plans.html","d":"A Store Plan gives a store one store code and a number of seats. A cashier types the store code once, and PLUed is unlocked on that phone with nothing to pay.","b":"store plans and store codes a store plan gives a store one store code and a number of seats. a cashier types the store code once, and plued is unlocked on that phone with nothing to pay. a store code is not a store pack the store code unlocks the app. the store pack adds your store's own codes. they are two separate things, each with its own qr code: the pack qr comes from the store pack builder , and the store code poster comes from your store page. a store on a store plan posts both. how a cashier uses the store code the cashier taps i have a store code on the setup page at first launch. later, the same entry is did your store give you a code? , under any locked level or under settings > market access > unlock everything . the cashier types the code, or taps scan the poster and points the camera at the poster's qr code. on an iphone or ipad, a second sheet from apple opens, and the cashier enters the same store code there. when the phone is unlocked, settings shows licensed to with your store's name. the store code needs version 1.2 or later of the app. seats a seat is used the first time a phone unlocks with the store code. typing the code again on the same phone uses no extra seat. a phone that unlocks keeps its unlock. it stays unlocked if the plan is not renewed or if more seats are added. your store page shows how many seats are in use. each time the plan renews, the seat count starts again from zero. phones unlocked in the year before stay unlocked and no longer count. when every seat is in use the next cashier who enters the store code sees all of your store's seats are in use. ask your manager to add more. under the message, tell your manager opens the phone's share sheet with a short note the cashier can send you. add seats from your store page. the store code stays the same. plued also emails your store's address when most of your seats are in use, and when a cashier could not join because no seat was left."},{"t":"Store pack spreadsheet columns","u":"admin/r_pack_spreadsheet.html","d":"The Store Pack Builder reads a .csv file or the first sheet of an .xlsx workbook. The first row names the columns, and each row after it is one code.","b":"store pack spreadsheet columns the store pack builder reads a .csv file or the first sheet of an .xlsx workbook. the first row names the columns, and each row after it is one code. table 1. columns column required what goes in it other headers read as this column code yes the standard plu or the store's own code: 3 to 5 digits, numbers only. plu, plu number, sku, item, item code name yes the item name cashiers see, up to 40 characters. plu description, item name, item description category yes a value that starts with fruit or veg , such as vegetable . any other value is filed as other. dept, department, dept no size no a size word from the size table below. none description no what the item looks like, such as \"large green apple, waxy skin\". the builder uses it with the name to choose a picture. it is not stored in the pack. desc, appearance, looks how headers are read headers are read in english. capital letters, spaces, underscores and hyphens do not matter, so item code and item_code are the same. a file with a description column and no name column uses the description column as the name. many register exports name the item this way. columns the builder does not know are ignored. table 2. size words word in the file size in the pack xs, extra small, xsmall xs s, sm, small s m, med, medium m l, lg, large l xl, extra large, xlarge xl blank, each, ea, all, all sizes, n/a, na, none no size what happens to each row a standard plu the row takes the plued picture and section for that code. a store's own code the builder picks the closest picture from the name and the description. check its picture and its section in the builder. a blank row skipped without a message. a code that is not 3 to 5 digits skipped. the result box names the row, for example row 9: code 123456 is not 3-5 digits. another category imported as other. the result box says so, for example row 7: category [deli] mapped to other. an unknown size word imported with no size. a message on the row asks you to pick a size or leave it blank for all sizes. a name that is too long imported as written. step 4 lists it under still to do before you can share until you shorten it. the same code twice in the file the later row updates the earlier one. a code already in the builder the row in the builder is updated with the file's name, category and size. no second row is added. a missing required column nothing is imported. the message names the missing column. row numbers in the messages count the header row as row 1 and leave out blank rows. in an excel workbook only the first sheet is read. excel drops a zero at the start of a number, so format the code column as text before you type or paste codes that start with 0. example a short file with two standard plus and one store code: code,name,category,size,description 4011,bananas,fruit,each,classic yellow bananas 4225,hass avocado,fruit,large,large dark pebbly avocado 830,cut watermelon bowl,deli,,red seedless watermelon cut in cubes the first two rows come in marked in plued . the third is a store code with a category the builder does not know, so it comes in as other, with a picture chosen from its name and description. check its picture and its section."},{"t":"Build a store pack","u":"admin/t_build_store_pack.html","d":"Type your store's codes into the Store Pack Builder one row at a time. Codes that PLUed already teaches fill in their own row.","b":"build a store pack type your store's codes into the store pack builder one row at a time. codes that plued already teaches fill in their own row. before you begin a computer or tablet with a web browser and an internet connection. your store's name and your list of produce codes. procedure in a web browser, open plued.app /pack . the store pack builder opens. it runs in the browser and needs no account. under store name , type the name your cashiers know. use up to 30 characters, with no single word over 16 letters. tap next → . step 2, add your codes , opens with one empty row. in the code box, type a code of 3 to 5 digits. if plued teaches the code, the row fills in the name, size, category, section and picture, and shows in plued . the builder fills only empty fields. anything you typed first stays. for one of your store's own codes, type the item name in the name box. use up to 40 characters. a code can appear in the pack once. a second row with the same code shows duplicate code. the builder picks the closest picture from the plued catalog. choose fruit , veg or other , and a size if the code is for one size. open the section menu and pick the aisle the item belongs to. to make your own section, pick + new section… , type a name of up to 32 characters, and tap add . to rename a section for every row in it, pick rename section… . check the picture on the row. to change it, tap the picture or change . the use a plued image box opens with suggestions and a search box. tap the picture closest to your item. a row with no picture shows check graphic and a use plued image button. optional: if no picture fits one of your store's own codes, tap request a graphic . describe what the item looks like in up to 200 characters, for example \"yellow cherry with a red blush, sold loose\", and tap request . keep the closest picture on the row until the new one is ready. the request is sent when you share the pack. request a graphic shows only for a code that plued does not teach, once the row has a code and a name. the row shows graphic requested . tap add code and repeat steps 4 to 9 for each item. optional: on step 3, practice lists , tap add practice list . type a list name , tap items , tick the items for the list, and tap done . your own codes are listed first. results step 4, share with your team , reads ready to share . if it reads still to do before you can share , tap a line in its list to go to the field that needs a change."},{"t":"Import a spreadsheet into a store pack","u":"admin/t_import_spreadsheet.html","d":"Bring a long list of codes into the Store Pack Builder from a CSV file or an Excel workbook instead of typing each row. Every row that comes in gets a picture to check.","b":"import a spreadsheet into a store pack bring a long list of codes into the store pack builder from a csv file or an excel workbook instead of typing each row. every row that comes in gets a picture to check. before you begin your produce list as a .csv or .xlsx file. most register and back-office exports work as they are. the first row of the file names the columns. the file needs a code column, a name column and a category column. procedure in a web browser, open plued.app /pack . the store pack builder opens. it runs in the browser and needs no account. under store name , type your store's name. tap next → to open step 2, add your codes . tap import csv / xlsx and choose your file. the same row of buttons has template.csv and template.xlsx , empty files with the right columns. the rows of your file appear in the table. a message at the bottom of the screen says for how many codes the builder matched a picture. read the result box under the buttons. it says how many rows were imported and how many were skipped, with one line for each row that needs your attention. for example, row 9: code 123456 is not 3-5 digits. names a row that was left out. check the picture on each of your store's own codes. rows marked in plued already have their own picture and section. for other rows the builder chose the closest picture from the name and the description. tap a picture to pick a better one. a row marked check graphic has no picture yet. open the section menu on each of your store's own codes and pick its aisle. decide whether to correct the file and import it again. if then you corrected rows in the file repeat step 4. a code that is already in the table is updated in place, so no row is added twice. the table is right the task is complete. results every usable row of the file is in the table. when nothing is left to check, the line under store codes ends with everything has a graphic and a section. ready to share."},{"t":"Request your store's logo","u":"admin/t_request_store_logo.html","d":"Type your store's website in the Store Pack Builder, and PLUed adds the store's logo to your pack. The request is free, and you never upload a picture.","b":"request your store's logo type your store's website in the store pack builder , and plued adds the store's logo to your pack. the request is free, and you never upload a picture. before you begin a store pack in the store pack builder . your store's own website, with the logo on it. plued adds only a logo your store may use. procedure in a web browser, open plued.app /pack . the store pack builder opens. it runs in the browser and needs no account. on step 1, name your store , find want your store’s logo in the app? (optional) under the store name. type your store's website, for example www.example.com . share the pack from step 4, share with your team . the request is sent with the pack. after a few days, open your pack in the builder again and read the line under the website box. if the line says then we got your request. we check each website ourselves, so allow a few days. the request is still waiting. check again later. your logo is in the app. the logo is shown small under the line. nothing more to do. a note from plued : read the note. it says what is needed from you. your store sets its logo on its store plan status page. your store has a store plan. upload the logo on your store page instead. results the logo shows on your store's card on home in every cashier's app, beside your store's name on the import store pack screen, and on your store's chip in the library for a cashier with two or more stores. a wide logo that spells out the store's name runs across the top of a wider card on home . cashiers who already have your pack get the logo by itself, usually within a day. they do not need to tap update available ."},{"t":"Share a store pack","u":"admin/t_share_store_pack.html","d":"Publish the pack from step 4 of the Store Pack Builder to get its share link and QR code. Cashiers open the link or scan the code to add the pack to their app.","b":"share a store pack publish the pack from step 4 of the store pack builder to get its share link and qr code. cashiers open the link or scan the code to add the pack to their app. before you begin the pack is open in the store pack builder and step 4 reads ready to share . an internet connection. about this task every shared pack sends a copy to plued , which checks it before its link appears. the check reads every name in the pack, in every language. procedure open step 4, share with your team . the share button reads publishing… while the pack is checked. decide what step 4 shows when the check ends. if then a qr code and copy share link continue with step 5. one name needs a small change before your pack can be shared. , a message about a few names, or one name is too long for the app. continue with step 3. couldn't check the pack just now, so it can't be shared yet. wait a minute, tap retry , and repeat this step. tap go to it . the builder opens the name, with a short note under it such as please try a different name here. or please shorten this name. type a different or shorter name, and go back to step 4. the check runs again by itself. if you think the name was fine, tap let us know. under the message. the message goes away, and the qr code and copy share link appear. tap copy share link and send the link to your cashiers by text or email. the builder shows share link copied . the link starts with plued.app /p/ . optional: show the qr code on your screen, or take a screenshot of it and print it for the break room. tap download .plupack and keep the file as a backup. results a cashier scans the qr code with the phone's camera or taps the link, and the app imports the pack. in the app, the cashier can also open library > import pack and tap scan qr , paste the link and tap import , or tap open .plupack file . the app then shows store pack imported with the number of codes and your store's name. anyone with the link can open the pack, so treat the qr code like a handout."},{"t":"Update a store pack","u":"admin/t_update_store_pack.html","d":"Reopen a pack you already shared, change it, and share it again. The pack keeps its link and QR code, so printed QR codes keep working.","b":"update a store pack reopen a pack you already shared, change it, and share it again. the pack keeps its link and qr code, so printed qr codes keep working. before you begin one of these: the browser you built the pack in. the pack's share link. the pack's .plupack file. procedure in a web browser, open plued.app /pack . the store pack builder opens. it runs in the browser and needs no account. decide whether the builder shows your pack. in the browser you built the pack in, the pack reopens by itself. if then your pack is open continue with step 5. the builder is empty or shows another pack continue with step 3. under already have a pack? , tap open from share link . if you have the file instead of the link, tap open a .plupack file , choose the file, and continue with step 5. paste the share link and tap open . the builder opens the pack with its codes, practice lists and pictures. make your changes. to add a code, tap add code . to remove a code, tap the delete row button (an x) beside the row's size menu. the code also leaves every practice list it was in. change names, pictures, sections and practice lists as you did when you built the pack. open step 4, share with your team , and wait while the share button reads publishing… . the pack publishes again under the same link and qr code. ask your cashiers to open library > import pack and tap update available beside your pack. a pack update does not reach the phones by itself. a store logo is the exception: a logo added later arrives without a tap. results after a cashier taps update available , the codes you added are on the phone and the codes you removed are gone from it. the cashier's practice history stays. a code that a cashier removed on the phone stays removed when the pack updates. what to do next caution: start over is for a different store. it clears the builder, and the next pack you share gets a new link. a pack you already shared stays shared."},{"t":"Concept","u":"glossary/g_concept.html","d":"","b":"concept one kind of produce, such as hass avocados. a concept owns one or more codes, one for each size, region, growing method or form that has its own code."},{"t":"Density Score","u":"glossary/g_density_score.html","d":"","b":"density score a number from 0 to 99 that rates how nutrient-rich a produce item is, shown in four bands: powerhouse, strong, everyday and treat."},{"t":"Most Common","u":"glossary/g_most_common.html","d":"","b":"most common the 120 concepts a store rings most often, taught first in ten levels. level 1 is free."},{"t":"Organic code","u":"glossary/g_organic_code.html","d":"","b":"organic code the code for the organic version of an item: a 9 followed by the item's 4-digit code. for example, 94011."},{"t":"PLU code","u":"glossary/g_plu_code.html","d":"","b":"plu code a 4-digit number that identifies a fresh produce item at the register. standard codes run from 3000 to 4999 and are assigned by the international federation for produce standards (ifps)."},{"t":"PLUzzle","u":"glossary/g_pluzzle.html","d":"","b":"pluzzle a daily puzzle. you guess the day's code in 6 tries. every player gets the same puzzle."},{"t":"Quick Play","u":"glossary/g_quick_play.html","d":"","b":"quick play a timed game in which produce rides a checkout belt and you type each item's code before it reaches the end."},{"t":"Seat","u":"glossary/g_seat.html","d":"","b":"seat one phone unlocked with a store code. a store plan has a set number of seats."},{"t":"Star","u":"glossary/g_star.html","d":"","b":"star a mark on each code that says your store carries it. codes start starred. a code with its star off leaves your flashcards and your mastery count."},{"t":"Store code","u":"glossary/g_store_code.html","d":"","b":"store code the term has two meanings in the app. in the library, a store code is a produce code a store uses for its own items, added by hand or from a store pack. on the unlock sheet, a store code is the code a store gives its cashiers with a store plan: entering it once unlocks the whole app on that phone."},{"t":"Store pack","u":"glossary/g_store_pack.html","d":"","b":"store pack a set of a store's own codes and names, built by a manager or trainer in the store pack builder and shared with cashiers as a link, a qr code or a file."},{"t":"About PLUed","u":"overview/c_about_plued.html","d":"PLUed is a training app for grocery cashiers. It teaches the 4-digit PLU codes that cashiers type at the register for fresh produce.","b":"about plued plued is a training app for grocery cashiers. it teaches the 4-digit plu codes that cashiers type at the register for fresh produce. each produce item in plued has a picture, its name and its codes. you study with flashcards and practice on a moving checkout belt. the app starts with the items a store rings most often and adds the rest over time. what the app holds plued 1.2.3 holds 1,116 produce items, grouped into 899 produce concepts. a concept is one kind of produce, such as hass avocados. one concept can own several codes for different sizes, regions or growing methods. where it runs the app runs on iphone and ipad, on android phones and tablets, and on amazon fire tablets. a web demo runs in a browser at plued.app /demo . the web demo has the free tier only, with no camera and no pack import. about this help this help has these guides: the user guide, for cashiers and shoppers. the admin guide, for store managers and trainers who prepare a store's codes."},{"t":"How PLU codes work","u":"overview/c_plu_codes.html","d":"A PLU code is a 4-digit number that identifies a fresh produce item at the register. The International Federation for Produce Standards (IFPS) assigns the standard codes.","b":"how plu codes work a plu code is a 4-digit number that identifies a fresh produce item at the register. the international federation for produce standards (ifps) assigns the standard codes. standard codes standard codes run from 3000 to 4999. the same code means the same item in every store that uses the standard list. for example, 4011 is bananas. note: for the organic version of any code, add a 9 in front of it. for example, 4011 becomes 94011. one item, several codes an item can have a separate code for each of these: size small, medium and large fruit of one variety can each have their own code. for navel oranges, 4012 is large, 3107 is medium and 4013 is small. region some produce has one code in the east and central united states and another in the west. growing method or form some items have separate codes for how they are grown or how they are sold, such as loose or in a bunch. each of these codes is its own answer. entering the code for a different size counts as a miss. store codes a store can also use its own codes for items that have no standard code, or for items it prices its own way. in the library , plued calls these store codes. a store shares them with its cashiers in a store pack. the code a store gives its cashiers with a store plan is a different thing. it unlocks the app and is not a produce code. retired and restricted codes ifps retires a code now and then, and restricts a few from use in the united states and canada. the app shows such a code with a retired or non-us label and leaves it out of practice. if your store still uses one, star it to add it back to your training."},{"t":"Who uses PLUed","u":"overview/c_who_uses_plued.html","d":"Cashiers learn the codes. Shoppers look up produce and its nutrition. Store managers and trainers prepare their store's codes for the cashiers.","b":"who uses plued cashiers learn the codes. shoppers look up produce and its nutrition. store managers and trainers prepare their store's codes for the cashiers. table 1. roles role what they do in plued guide cashier studies flashcards, practices on the checkout belt, and learns the store's own codes. user guide shopper scans a sticker or types a name to see an item, its density score and its nutrition. user guide store manager or trainer builds a store pack with the store's codes, shares it, and gives cashiers a store code that unlocks the app. admin guide at first launch the app asks whether you work a register or are shopping. you can change the answer later in settings > using plued as ."},{"t":"The concept card","u":"user/c_concept_card.html","d":"A concept card shows one kind of produce and every code it owns. You open it from the Library, from a scan, or from a card on Home.","b":"the concept card a concept card shows one kind of produce and every code it owns. you open it from the library , from a scan, or from a card on home . picture, name and score the card starts with the produce picture, its name, its family and its density score. when you open the card by scanning a sticker, a line under the picture names the code you scanned, such as you scanned 4011 , and that code's row carries a scanned tag. codes the codes section has one row for each code, shown as a large number. the line organic = 9 + plu above the rows states the organic rule once. chips on each row say what makes that code different: size, such as s, l or all sizes region: east/central or west grow method, such as greenhouse or field form, such as bunch or seedless codes used everywhere come first. codes for one region follow under a region heading. if you set a region, the card leaves out the other region's codes. each row also has a star. a starred code is part of your study set. labels on a code row known you know this code. a code counts after a correct answer in under 5 seconds with no hint. later the app teaches the most common size or region of an item first. the other codes wait until you know that one. retired or non-us ifps retired the code, or restricts it from use in the united states and canada. the code is shown for reference and left out of practice. still in use a retired code that you starred back into your training. store pack or my store a store code from an imported pack, or one you added yourself. mastery and note mastery counts how many of the codes you study are known, for example 2 of 3 studied codes known . a note card gives a coaching tip when one exists. actions study opens flashcards for this item. practice starts a short belt drill on it. compare opens the nutrition explorer with this item on the board. viewing the card and compare are free. study and practice need the full app unless the item is in level 1. on a screen at least 600 points wide, the card has two columns. a shopper sees the nutrition first and the codes after it."},{"t":"The Density Score","u":"user/c_density_score.html","d":"The Density Score is a number from 0 to 99 that says how much nutrition a produce item gives compared with other produce. It is free for everyone.","b":"the density score the density score is a number from 0 to 99 that says how much nutrition a produce item gives compared with other produce. it is free for everyone. where you see it the score sits under the item's name on its concept card. tap the score for the full breakdown, or tap the information icon beside it for a short explanation. the explanation is stored in the app and opens without a connection. in the library , the nutrition view orders every item by its score. what goes into it table 1. parts of the score part what it measures nutrient concentration, 50% how packed the food is with nutrients once the water is set aside. more sugar lowers it. nutrition per serving, 30% how much nutrition a typical serving gives, as % daily value. low calories, 10% fewer calories per bite scores higher. plant compounds, 10% natural plant compounds beyond vitamins. the four bands powerhouse 75 to 99 strong 50 to 74 everyday 25 to 49 treat under 25 a lower score means less nutrition per bite. it never means that a food is bad. items with no score a few items have no score, such as decorative items, wrapper leaves and store codes the app has no data for. for these the card shows a line in place of the score, for example no density score with the reason. the app never shows a missing score as 0. note: level 1, pluzzle , the density score and the nutrition tools are free. other study needs the one-time unlock or a store code."},{"t":"Free and full access","u":"user/r_free_and_full.html","d":"Part of PLUed is free for everyone. A one-time purchase, or a store code from your store, unlocks the rest. There is no subscription.","b":"free and full access part of plued is free for everyone. a one-time purchase, or a store code from your store, unlocks the rest. there is no subscription. table 1. what each tier includes feature free full level 1: study, practice and play yes yes pluzzle yes yes density score and the nutrition explorer yes yes browsing the library and every concept card yes yes scanning a sticker yes yes looking at your store's pack yes yes levels 2 to 10, store sections and recipe sets shown, locked yes flashcards and games on every item no yes practicing your store's pack no yes unlocking tap a locked level, or tap unlock everything under market access in settings . the unlock the whole market sheet shows the price from your app store. the sheet also opens by itself when you finish level 1. if the app store does not answer, the sheet shows store unavailable . check your connection and tap retry . restore purchases if you bought the full app on another device with the same app store account, tap restore purchases on the unlock sheet or in settings ."},{"t":"Settings","u":"user/r_settings.html","d":"To open Settings, tap the gear icon on Home. This table lists every group and what it does, from top to bottom.","b":"settings to open settings , tap the gear icon on home . this table lists every group and what it does, from top to bottom. table 1. settings groups group what it does market access shows whether the full app is unlocked. if it is not, it has restore purchases and unlock everything . a phone unlocked by a store code on android or a fire tablet shows licensed to store and remove store license , which takes the store's unlock off this phone. your store invite your store opens your phone's share sheet with a message that sends your manager the free store pack builder . build a store pack opens the store pack builder in your browser. my store data lists the packs, codes and groups you added, and removes any of them. using plued as register or shopping . changes what home shows. what you have learned stays. appearance system , light or dark . system follows your device. language system , english or español (beta) . the change takes effect at once. my region east / central , west or i'm not sure, show all codes . sets which codes you study. the last choice turns off the region filter. setup how plued works opens the in-app guide. replay setup runs the first-launch setup again. the app version, 1.2.3 , is at the bottom of the sheet."},{"t":"Stars in Quick Play","u":"user/r_star_system.html","d":"Each Quick Play session starts with 5 stars. This table lists how each answer changes your stars.","b":"stars in quick play each quick play session starts with 5 stars. this table lists how each answer changes your stars. table 1. star changes per answer what you did stars item goes to break time typed the right code within 3 seconds, no hint +2 no typed the right code after 3 seconds, no hint +1 no tapped the item's tag ( what kind? ), then typed the right code 0 no tapped lookup -1 yes retyped the code that lookup showed 0 already added typed a wrong code, including the code for another size or region of the same item -1 yes let the item reach the end of the belt -1 yes limits stars never go below 0. at 0, break time starts. after break time, you go back to the belt with 3 stars. practice mode uses no stars."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","u":"user/r_troubleshooting.html","d":"This table lists problems cashiers and shoppers report, what causes them and how to fix them. Quoted text is what the app shows.","b":"troubleshooting this table lists problems cashiers and shoppers report, what causes them and how to fix them. quoted text is what the app shows. table 1. problems and fixes problem cause fix the unlock sheet shows store unavailable . the app store did not answer within about 10 seconds. check your connection and tap retry . you bought the full app, but this device is locked. the purchase was made on another device. tap restore purchases in settings , signed in to the same app store account. a pack link opens a web page and not the app. the link was opened on a device without the app, or the device did not hand it to the app. copy the link. in the app, open import store pack , paste the link and tap import . could not reach the pack. check your connection. a pack link or qr code needs a connection the first time. connect and import again, or ask your trainer for the .plupack file. this pack is no longer available. the pack was removed. ask your trainer for a new link. camera scanning isn’t available here. paste the link. the device has no camera the app can use. paste the pack link in import store pack . the sticker scanner shows no code found yet. the sticker is too close, moving or in glare. hold it about a hand's length away and keep it still. if it still fails, tap type it instead . the scanner says a code is not in plued . the code is a store's own code. import your store's pack, or tap add \" code \" as a store code . a code you need is missing from a concept card. your region setting hides the other region's codes. in settings , under my region , tap your region or i'm not sure, show all codes . a code never comes up in flashcards or games. its star is off, or it is a retired or non-us code. open its concept card and tap the star on its row. the weak chip shows not enough data yet . fewer than 10 answers are on record. keep studying. weak spots start after 10 answers. that code was not recognized. check the spelling with your manager. the store code was typed wrong. check the code with your manager, or tap scan the poster . all of your store's seats are in use. ask your manager to add more. every seat on the store's plan is taken. tap tell your manager . the code works once the store adds seats."},{"t":"Unlock the app with a store code","u":"user/t_enter_store_code.html","d":"If your store set up PLUed for its cashiers, it has one store code for everyone. Enter it once to unlock the whole app on your phone.","b":"unlock the app with a store code if your store set up plued for its cashiers, it has one store code for everyone. enter it once to unlock the whole app on your phone. before you begin your store gave you its store code, on a poster or from your manager. the app needs a connection to check the code. procedure tap any locked level. you can also open settings and, under market access , tap unlock everything . the unlock the whole market sheet opens. tap did your store give you a code? enter your store code opens. type the store code in the store code box. to fill it in from your store's poster instead, tap scan the poster and point the camera at the poster's qr code. tap unlock . on android and fire tablets, the app says welcome to the store team. the whole market is unlocked. on iphone or ipad, paste the code in apple's box. the app checks your store's seats, copies the code for you and then opens apple's redeem sheet. follow apple's sheet to finish. results if the app shows all of your store's seats are in use. ask your manager to add more. , every seat on your store's plan is taken. tap tell your manager to send your manager a short note through your phone's share sheet. your code works as soon as the store adds seats. each phone uses one seat the first time it unlocks. entering the code again on the same phone uses no extra seat. a phone that is already unlocked shows a note instead of the box and uses no seat."},{"t":"Import your store's pack","u":"user/t_import_store_pack.html","d":"A store pack holds a store's own codes, its practice lists and the pictures for each item. Import the pack your trainer shared to study your store's codes.","b":"import your store's pack a store pack holds a store's own codes, its practice lists and the pictures for each item. import the pack your trainer shared to study your store's codes. before you begin a trainer or manager shared a pack with you as a qr code, a link or a .plupack file. a qr code or link needs a connection the first time you import it. about this task if you tap a pack link on a phone that has the app, the app opens import store pack and starts the import by itself. continue with step 5. procedure at the bottom of the screen, tap library . tap import pack . before you have any pack, home also has an add a store pack row that opens the same screen. in the shopper view, tap add your store on home . the import store pack screen opens. decide how you received the pack. if then a qr code tap scan qr and point the camera at the qr code. the import starts when the code is read. continue with step 5. a link or code in a message paste it in the store pack link or code box. continue with step 4. a .plupack file tap open .plupack file and choose the file. the import starts when you choose it. continue with step 5. tap import . if codes already in your store opens, tap keep both or replace mine . this happens when the pack uses a code you already have from another pack or added yourself. on store pack imported , tap ok . the message lists how many codes and practice lists came in. results your store's items appear on home under your store's name, and carry a store badge in the library . when the trainer updates the pack, update available shows beside it on import store pack . note: looking at your store's pack is free. practicing it needs the full app or a store code."},{"t":"Look up a PLU code","u":"user/t_look_up_plu.html","d":"Search the Library by name, code or other name to find an item and open its concept card.","b":"look up a plu code search the library by name, code or other name to find an item and open its concept card. procedure at the bottom of the screen, tap library . tap the search box, name, plu or alias . type a name, a code, an organic code or another name for the item. for example, type banana , 4011 or 94011 . words can be in any order. when the app is in spanish, search by the spanish name. if you typed a full code that belongs to one item, its concept card opens by itself. otherwise the grid shows the matching items. tap the item's card in the grid. if only one item matches, you can tap the search key on the keyboard instead. the concept card opens with the item's codes. results note: for the organic version of any code, add a 9 in front of it. for example, 4011 becomes 94011. if nothing matches, the library says so. a cashier can then tap add \" search \" as a store code to add the item as a store code."},{"t":"Play the daily PLUzzle","u":"user/t_play_pluzzle.html","d":"PLUzzle shows one produce item a day, the same for every player. You have 6 guesses to find its 4-digit code. It is free for everyone.","b":"play the daily pluzzle pluzzle shows one produce item a day, the same for every player. you have 6 guesses to find its 4-digit code. it is free for everyone. procedure on home , tap the pluzzle row at the top. today's item appears with guess the plu . type a 4-digit code on the keypad. any 4-digit number is a valid guess. tap the check mark key. each digit of your guess changes color: green: the right digit in the right place. yellow: a digit in the code, in another place. tan: a digit that is not in the code. repeat steps 2 and 3 until you find the code or use all 6 guesses. the result sheet opens with your streak and stats. optional: tap share results . the shared text has the puzzle number, your score, a link to the puzzle and a grid of colored squares. it does not show the code. optional: tap practice this produce to drill today's item. practice on an item outside level 1 needs the full app. what to do next a new puzzle comes each day. the pluzzle row on home shows whether you played today and your current streak."},{"t":"Play Quick Play on the belt","u":"user/t_play_quick_play.html","d":"In Quick Play, produce rides a checkout belt and you type each code before the item reaches the end. You earn and lose stars as you go.","b":"play quick play on the belt in quick play , produce rides a checkout belt and you type each code before the item reaches the end. you earn and lose stars as you go. procedure on home , on the continue card, tap quick play . you can also start it from a level's sheet, or from the bar at the bottom of the library , where it plays up to 20 of the items in view. a countdown runs, and the first item comes onto the belt. type the item's code on the keypad. the app checks the answer when the last digit is in. if you are not sure of the item, tap its tag or the what kind? pill under it. the app names the item and shows its details, without the code. a correct answer after this earns no stars. if you do not know the code, tap lookup . lookup costs a star and shows the code. the belt stops. type the code that lookup showed. the prompt says retype this code . the game does not go on until you type the exact code. the retype earns no stars. if a coaching sheet opens after a wrong answer, tap got it! . the sheet shows your code beside the right one. to compare the two items, tap see them side by side . note: each code is scored on its own. a code for another size, growing method or form of the same produce counts as a miss. a code that differs only by region is accepted when the two codes are listed as regional twins. when your stars run out, work through the break time flashcards. break time shows the items you missed or looked up. when you finish, tap back to game . you return to the belt with 3 stars. on the receipt at the end, tap play again , practice missed ( n ) or done . what to do next after about 15 minutes of play, a sheet suggests a stopping point. tap keep going or take a break . in practice mode the belt has no stars and no break time, and the item's name is shown."},{"t":"Scan a produce sticker","u":"user/t_scan_sticker.html","d":"Point the camera at a PLU sticker to open the item's concept card. The scanner reads the code on the phone, and no picture leaves the device.","b":"scan a produce sticker point the camera at a plu sticker to open the item's concept card. the scanner reads the code on the phone, and no picture leaves the device. before you begin the scanner runs in the iphone, ipad, android and fire tablet apps. the web demo has no camera. procedure open the scanner from one of these places: on home , on the scan a sticker card, tap open scanner . in the shopper view, tap scan . in the library , tap the round scan button at the right end of the empty search box. the camera view opens. hold the sticker about a hand's length from the camera, 8 to 12 inches. closer is not better. the camera cannot focus on a sticker that is only a few inches away. hold the sticker still until the item opens. there is no shutter button. the scanner reads the code twice before it opens anything. between the two reads the line under the frame says read 4011. hold steady. the concept card opens. a line under the picture names the code you scanned. an organic sticker opens the conventional item. results if the scanner cannot finish, the line under the frame tells you why: no code found yet. after four tries or about six seconds with no code, move the sticker back to a hand's length and hold it still. the scanner keeps trying. to type the code instead, tap type it instead . the library search opens. 7034 is not in plued . the sticker has a code the app does not have, often a store's own code. a cashier can tap add \"7034\" as a store code . a shopper sees the line only."},{"t":"Set up PLUed at first launch","u":"user/t_set_up_first_run.html","d":"The first time you open the app, it asks whether you work a register or are shopping. Cashiers then pick a region and an experience level and can load their store's codes.","b":"set up plued at first launch the first time you open the app, it asks whether you work a register or are shopping. cashiers then pick a region and an experience level and can load their store's codes. about this task every choice on these pages can change later in settings . to leave the setup at any point, tap skip . skipping sets you up as a cashier with all regions shown. procedure optional: to change the language, tap en or es at the top right of the welcome page. under what brings you to plued ? , tap i work a register or i'm shopping . tap continue . if you chose i'm shopping , the app skips to the last page. continue with step 8. under where do you ring? , tap east / central , west or show all . the app hides the codes that apply only in the other region. if you are not sure, tap show all . under how much produce have you rung? , tap new or pro . this choice only suggests where to start. it does not lock anything. under got a store pack? , decide whether your store gave you anything. if then a trainer shared a qr code, a link or a file with the store's codes tap import now . your store gave you a store code tap i have a store code . you have neither continue with step 7. tap get started . on your stall is set , tap enter the market . home opens. what to do next appearance and language follow your device. to change them, or to run this setup again, use settings ."},{"t":"Choose the codes you study","u":"user/t_star_codes.html","d":"Every code has a star. Turn a star off for a code your store does not use, and the code leaves your flashcards, games and mastery count.","b":"choose the codes you study every code has a star. turn a star off for a code your store does not use, and the code leaves your flashcards, games and mastery count. before you begin open the concept card of the item. about this task every code starts starred. a retired or non-us code is left out of practice. if your store still uses one, you can star it back in. procedure in the codes section, find the row of the code. tap the star on that row. a filled star turns to an outline, and the code leaves your study set. an outlined star fills in, and the code comes back. optional: to study a code with a retired or non-us chip, tap the star on its row. the app asks your store still uses code ? optional: tap add to my training . to keep the code out of practice, tap cancel instead. the chip changes to still in use . the code is back in your flashcards, games and mastery count. what to do next the starred chip in flashcards studies only the codes you keep starred."},{"t":"Study with flashcards","u":"user/t_study_flashcards.html","d":"Each flashcard is one produce item. You type its codes from memory, and the app brings each card back when you are about to forget it.","b":"study with flashcards each flashcard is one produce item. you type its codes from memory, and the app brings each card back when you are about to forget it. procedure at the bottom of the screen, tap flashcards . the review deck opens. the front of a card asks what are the codes? and shows one empty slot for each code you study. optional: tap a chip to narrow the deck. chip cards in the deck all every card that is due for review. starred only the codes you keep starred. weak the codes you keep missing. with fewer than 10 answers on record, it shows not enough data yet . type each code on the keypad. each slot takes only its own code. a slot you get wrong keeps your entry in red, with the correct code under it. the card turns over and shows all its codes. swipe left for the next card. after the last card, the deck starts again from the first. results if you do not know a card, tap it to turn it over before you answer. then rate yourself missed or tough . a card you turned over first does not count toward known. note: the chips appear only on the deck you open from flashcards . flashcards opened from a concept card, a level or the library study exactly that set."}];
